{"id": 44, "ts": 1781203612.393187, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress handling, but the lack of any concrete evidence on B\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation remains a critical gap for a long\u2011distance cockpit where teamwork is non\u2011negotiable. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC brings documented strengths that directly address those gaps:\u202fC is described as\u202f100\u202f% reliable\u202fand\u202fcreates a positive atmosphere with his crew, which suggests solid crew cooperation.\u202fAdditionally, C \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d giving us at least some indication of decision quality in safety\u2011critical contexts. While C does have communication challenges and a reluctance to pursue further education, the positive crew dynamic and proven reliability outweigh B\u2019s pretentious tone and the complete absence of crew\u2011cooperation data. Therefore, I shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**."}
